1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Go is great at building and deploying services. Python has a vast ecosystem of libraries and applications.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
What if they could work together inside the same program?

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Pythago embeds CPython in Go executables built with CGO disabled, so both languages can call each other in one process.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:34,000
It starts with a Python distribution from python-build-standalone.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Pythago-dist fetches the distribution. On Linux and macOS, it uses bao to translate the Python runtime into a linkable image.

6
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:53,000
On Windows, the package bundles Python and glue DLLs. At startup, Pythago extracts them to a cache and loads them.

7
00:00:53,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Your Go application imports the generated package. It includes the runtime for the target platform and the standard library. System libraries are still required.

8
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Inside the executable, the py package manages the embedded interpreter and its Python objects.

9
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:24,000
A Go program can import a Python module, call its functions, and work with the returned values.

10
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Calls cross a small layer of C glue that handles the parts of CPython’s interface Go cannot call directly.

11
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:45,000
The conversation goes both ways: Python can call Go functions too, and errors can cross the boundary.

12
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Python needs more than an interpreter. It also needs modules, resources, and sometimes native extensions.

13
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:03,000
The standard library and application files can be served from a Go filesystem, including embedded files.

14
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:12,000
For larger dependencies, Pythago can use an environment on disk, with compatible packages and native extensions.

15
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Extension support depends on the operating system and the Python version and ABI.

16
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Go uses goroutines; CPython has its own rules about threads and interpreter state.

17
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Pythago coordinates entry into Python and attaches the appropriate Python thread state to the operating system thread.

18
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:50,000
On Linux and macOS, eligible Python threads run on goroutines locked to OS threads. On Windows, CPython starts its own threads.

19
00:02:50,000 --> 00:03:00,000
You choose a normal GIL build or an opt-in free-threaded Python build when generating the image.

20
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Now follow a request to a Python web application running inside a Go server.

21
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Go’s net/http accepts the request and passes it to Pythago’s ASGI handler.

22
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:31,000
The handler translates the request into ASGI events and calls the Python application.

23
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:42,000
For asynchronous work, Pythago’s aio package provides a Go-backed asyncio event loop.

24
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:54,000
The application sends its response through ASGI, and Go writes it back to the client.

25
00:03:54,000 --> 00:04:05,000
For synchronous Python web applications, Pythago also provides a WSGI handler.

26
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:14,000
A small pure-Python application can package its Python files and standard library with the executable.

27
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:23,000
Larger native stacks can instead use an environment on disk beside the application.

28
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Pythago supports Linux, macOS, and Windows on amd64 and arm64.

29
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Compatible native extensions can load from disk. Match the package to your operating system, architecture, and Python ABI.

30
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Pythago brings CPython into a Go executable, connects the two languages, and lets them share a process.

31
00:04:49,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Use Python’s ecosystem alongside Go’s networking and deployment model. Explore Pythago to see how the pieces fit together.
